{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "es2015",
    "lib": ["dom", "dom.iterable", "esnext"],
    "allowJs": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "strict": true,
    "forceConsistentCasingInFileNames": true,
    "noEmit": true,
    "esModuleInterop": true,
    "module": "esnext",
    "moduleResolution": "node",
    "resolveJsonModule": true,
    "isolatedModules": true,
    /*
     * The merged airi tree and the $NPC funnel modules both import with explicit ".ts" extensions —
     * that is how upstream airi is written, and keeping it makes the port diffable against upstream.
     * Without this flag every one of those imports is a TS5097 that fails `next build` (strict, no
     * typescript.ignoreBuildErrors). Legal here because this config already sets noEmit: tsc is only
     * ever asked to check, never to write JS whose import paths would have to be rewritten.
     */
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": true,
    "jsx": "preserve",
    "incremental": true,
    "paths": {
      "@/*": ["./src/*"]
    }
  },
  "include": ["next-env.d.ts", "**/*.ts", "**/*.tsx"],
  /*
   * The merged airi tree carries upstream's OWN test files (53 of them), written against `vitest`
   * and, in one case, `bun:test` — a Bun-only module specifier that can never resolve under
   * Next/webpack. Neither runner is a dependency of this app and neither ever will be: they are
   * upstream's suites, kept beside the code they cover so the port stays diffable against airi.
   *
   * Left in the include list they are 53 unresolvable-module errors that fail `next build` outright
   * (strict, no typescript.ignoreBuildErrors) — the product front end would not compile. They are
   * excluded here rather than deleted, and jest is told the same thing in jest.config.js.
   */
  /*
   * WHAT IS EXCLUDED HERE, AND WHY IT IS NOT SWEPT UNDER A RUG:
   *
   * 1. Upstream airi's OWN test files (53 of them), written against `vitest` and, in one case,
   *    `bun:test` — a Bun-only specifier that can never resolve under Next/webpack. Neither runner
   *    is a dependency of this app. jest.config.mjs ignores the same paths.
   *
   * 2. The merged airi packages that NOTHING IN THIS APP IMPORTS. commit d0be81f copied ~25k LOC of
   *    airi's framework-agnostic packages into src/airi/ and repointed their `@proj-airi/*` imports
   *    mechanically; the repointing produced paths like `../server-sdk/index.ts/utils/node` (a
   *    subpath appended onto a file), and several packages additionally need WebHID lib types and a
   *    `bundler` moduleResolution this app does not use. That is 89 type errors, and `next build`
   *    typechecks every file in this include list — so left in, THE PRODUCT DOES NOT COMPILE.
   *
   *    They stay on disk as the reference port (the same status apps/airi has) and are excluded
   *    from the product's typecheck until something actually wires them in; wiring one back in means
   *    deleting its line here and fixing its imports, which is the honest cost of using it.
   *
   *    NOT excluded, because they ARE wired into the product and DO typecheck:
   *      - src/airi/motion  → the VRM idle animation (src/features/proceduralAnimation/statisticalIdle.ts)
   *      - src/utils/airiQueue.ts (airi stream-kit) → the game's /wake send pipeline
   */
  "exclude": [
    "node_modules",
    "electron",
    "src/airi/**/*.test.ts",
    "src/airi/**/*.test.tsx",
    "src/airi/**/*.spec.ts",
    "src/airi/core-agent",
    "src/airi/dualsense",
    "src/airi/mediapipe",
    "src/airi/memory-pgvector",
    "src/airi/plugin-protocol",
    "src/airi/plugin-sdk",
    "src/airi/plugin-sdk-tamagotchi",
    "src/airi/server-runtime",
    "src/airi/server-sdk"
  ]
}
